{0 awskit-s3}

AWS S3 client surface for classic bucket/object storage operations, multipart
uploads, S3 presigned URLs, opaque bucket policy documents, and deterministic
simulation.

See {{:../../doc/awskit.html}[awskit]} for the pure core and runtime adapter
overview.

The public entrypoint is {!module:Awskit_s3}. Implementation modules, XML
codecs, request builders, and response parsers are private.

{1 Scope}

[awskit-s3] targets the regular AWS S3 service client shape: buckets,
objects, multipart uploads, bucket configuration, presigned object URLs, and
test simulation.

[awskit-s3] is optimized for common S3 application workloads, not exhaustive
parity with every Amazon S3 action. The priority path is object CRUD/list/copy,
metadata, tags, ranges, presigned URLs, multipart upload, common bucket
configuration, and production SDK behavior such as credentials, retries,
pagination, and streaming correctness.

The package intentionally does not include S3 Control. Account/control-plane
features such as access point administration, Storage Lens, Access Grants,
Batch Operations, Object Lambda administration, Multi-Region Access Point
administration, and Outposts administration do not belong in [awskit-s3].

The package also does not model S3-branded products that are not the classic
bucket/object API, such as S3 Tables, S3 Vectors, S3 Files, and S3 Metadata
table features.

AWS-only object-storage extensions such as directory buckets/S3 Express,
access points, and Multi-Region Access Points are future explicit models, not
part of the plain bucket/object API.

Bucket policy operations are S3 operations and are included. Policy documents
are opaque JSON payloads; this package does not build IAM policies or evaluate
IAM policy semantics.

{1 API Shape}

Object APIs are split into explicit layers:

{ul
  {li primitive streaming operations under [Object]}
  {li bounded in-memory helpers under [Object.Buffer]}
  {li local-path helpers under [Object.Transfer] in Unix-capable adapter
    packages}
}

Primitive operations never expose string bodies as the primary API. Upload
bodies and download readers come from the selected runtime adapter.

{1 Libraries}

{2 awskit-s3}

{!module:Awskit_s3} contains pure types, S3 endpoint configuration, standalone
presigned URL helpers, the runtime functor, and the deterministic simulator.

Main modules:

{ul
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Object} — object types, options, metadata records,
    checksums, preconditions, and object tagging result types}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Bucket} — bucket result types and bucket
    configuration records}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Multipart} — multipart upload identifiers, parts,
    options, and result records}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Presigned} — pure presigned URL generation}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Policy} — validated opaque bucket policy JSON
    payloads}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Sim} — in-memory S3 test surface}
  {li {!module:Awskit_s3.Make} — functor for wiring S3 operations to a custom
    {!module-type:Awskit.Runtime.S} implementation}
}

{2 awskit-s3.eio}

{!module:Awskit_s3_eio} provides a direct-style Eio adapter. Operations return
plain results. It also exposes local-path helpers under [Object.Transfer].

{2 awskit-s3.lwt}

{!module:Awskit_s3_lwt} provides a functor over [Cohttp_lwt.S.Client].
Operations return [Lwt.t].

{2 awskit-s3.lwt_unix}

{!module:Awskit_s3_lwt_unix} provides the ready-to-use Lwt + Unix adapter.
It can read credentials and region from the standard AWS environment variables
through the underlying [awskit.lwt_unix] runtime.

{1 Minimal Eio Example}

{[
open Eio.Std

let run env =
  Switch.run @@ fun sw ->
  let credentials =
    Awskit.Credentials.create_exn
      ~access_key_id:"AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE"
      ~secret_access_key:"wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY"
      ()
  in
  let region = Awskit.Region.of_string_exn "us-east-1" in
  let s3 = Awskit_s3_eio.create ~sw ~env ~region ~credentials () in
  match
    Awskit_s3_eio.Object.Buffer.put_string s3
      ~bucket:"my-bucket"
      ~key:"hello.txt"
      "Hello, S3!"
  with
  | Ok _ -> ()
  | Error err -> Fmt.epr "%a@." Awskit_s3.Error.pp err
]}

{1 Minimal Lwt Unix Example}

{[
let run () =
  let open Lwt.Syntax in
  match Awskit_s3_lwt_unix.create () with
  | Error err ->
      Lwt_io.eprintf "%s\n" (Awskit_s3.Error.to_string_hum err)
  | Ok s3 ->
      let* result =
        Awskit_s3_lwt_unix.Object.Buffer.get_string s3
          ~bucket:"my-bucket"
          ~key:"hello.txt"
          ~max_size:1_048_576L
          ()
      in
      match result with
      | Ok (_info, body) -> Lwt_io.printl body
      | Error err -> Lwt_io.eprintf "%a\n" Awskit_s3.Error.pp err
]}

